# Merge perfect, drop the rest

distill: skill_distill/captures/2026-08-22_cursor_orchestration-outside-editor.md

**Perfect** means all of: not draft, base is `main` / `dms-v2` / `dms-integrated-engine`, `mergeable=MERGEABLE`, no conflicts, and these checks are SUCCESS: `lint-type-test`, `base-install`, `protected-paths`, `rls-proof`, `secrets-scan`. Local `pytest -q` already ran green on the same SHA.

When a PR is perfect, squash-merge it. Do not wait for a human. Cloud-agent `gh` is read-only; CI job `auto-merge` is the merge. If that job cannot merge (review required), it enables GitHub auto-merge.

Do **not** merge when any required check failed, the PR is draft, dirty/behind, or it weakens a refusal / reclassifies hostile SQL / hand-edits `contract/*.json` / adds `_C2_ALLOWLIST` names. Those are not perfect.

## Merge tiers

Approved 2026-10-06 12:02 MYT (FAST LANE, relayed by Netie Lead). This section is the canonical tier text; other files point here.

Until #339 lands, the CI `auto-merge` job squash-merges any non-draft PR whose checks are green (the "Perfect" rule above) and does not look at the tier label, CLEAR or AGREE. That is why no PR leaves draft before its tier's pre-merge steps are done on its exact head, and why a `tier:full` PR stays draft until its manual squash.

1. **Scope.** `tier:fast` covers UI, docs, tests, cleanup, and features behind a flag that is off by default and byte-identical when off. Cleanup is fast only with BOTH an attic copy of what it removes AND a green import check (`lint-imports` and `tests/contract/test_import_boundaries.py`). Never fast, even when the change is test-only or data-only: anything touching the contract, auth or grants, keys, routing, prove pins (`279cbd85`), the import-linter invariants, abstain/WRONG behaviour, engine behaviour, or scoring and eval. That includes the hostile-SQL corpus, golden, held-out and scoring packs, and abstain fixtures. Everything else is `tier:full`. No label means `tier:full`. When unsure, use full. PR Bot bounces a `tier:fast` PR that touches a never-fast area to `tier:full`.
2. **`tier:fast` merge bar.** The steps and order of `AGENTS.md` rule 1, on one exact head: CI 5/5 SUCCESS (`lint-type-test`, `base-install`, `protected-paths`, `rls-proof`, `secrets-scan`), then a `PR Bot CLEAR @ <full 40-hex head>` comment, then one AGREE from a reviewer of a different model family than the writer that names its family, then squash-merge with `--match-head-commit <head>`. PR Bot's CLEAR attests the CI result on that head; it is a comment, not an extra review wait. The PR stays draft until CLEAR and AGREE are both on that head (`AGENTS.md` rule 2). Rule 1's post-merge Check (R-0003) and Lead Formal still follow; if R-0003 returns NO, revert the merge at once. #339 adds the CLEAR and AGREE comment formats to `AGENTS.md`.
3. **`tier:full` merge bar.** The PR stays draft throughout, until the manual squash: CI 5/5 SUCCESS on the exact head, then exact-head PR Bot CLEAR, then a different-family AGREE, then Check pre-merge, then Lead Formal, then a manual squash with `--match-head-commit <head>`. Check post-merge (R-0003) and Lead DONE/BLOCKED follow the merge. This is stricter than `AGENTS.md` rule 1: it adds Check pre-merge and Lead Formal ahead of the squash, and still runs rule 1's post-merge Check (R-0003) and Lead step, which reports DONE/BLOCKED.
4. **Exact head only.** Any head move (new commit, rebase, force-push) voids CLEAR and AGREE in both tiers. CLEAR and AGREE must name the full 40-hex head SHA; a short SHA never counts.
5. No CI check is weakened, skipped or made optional by either tier. Every existing invariant stays as-is: one writer per branch, nothing declared PASS, `DMS_L2_ENABLED=1` never committed, protected-paths rules. GitHub labels `tier:fast` and `tier:full` already exist in the repo.

## Remove useless work

- Do not add LangGraph, CrewAI, n8n, Money Gainer, or Outlier scraping.
- Do not keep a dead search box, duplicate blurb, or a parked item that is only "review this capture".
- Do not open a second orchestrator. Cortex already is the loop.
- Close or skip draft PRs that duplicate a landed fix. Do not pile drive-by refactors onto a green PR.
